Q: HTML email not rendering in flutter A: <pre><code> String _sanitizeHtml(String htmlContent) {
    try {
      // Parse and validate HTML
      final document = html_parser.parse(htmlContent);
      return document.body?.innerHtml ?? htmlContent; // Change here
    } catch (e) {
      debugPrint('HTML parsing error: $e');
      return htmlContent;
    }
  }
</code></pre>
<p><code>document.body.innerHtml</code> gets the content <em>inside</em> the <code>&lt;body&gt;</code> tag (HTML without the <code>&lt;body&gt;</code> tags), while <code>document.outerHtml</code> gets the <em>entire</em> document's HTML, including the <code>&lt;html&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;head&gt;</code>, and <code>&lt;body&gt;</code> tags, making <code>document.body.</code></p>
<h3>document.body.innerHtml</h3>
<ul>
<li><p><strong>What it is</strong>: Returns the HTML content <em>inside</em> the <code>&lt;body&gt;</code> element, as a string.</p>
</li>
<li><p><strong>Use case</strong>: To get or set only the visible content, like text, images, lists, etc., within the main part of the webpage, without the <code>&lt;html&gt;</code> or <code>&lt;body&gt;</code> tags themselves.</p>
</li>
<li><p><strong>Example</strong>: If your HTML is <code>&lt;html&gt;&lt;body&gt;&lt;h1&gt;Title&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;Text&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</code>, <code>document.body.innerHtml</code> would give you <code>&lt;h1&gt;Title&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;Text&lt;/p&gt;</code>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3>document.outerHtml</h3>
<ul>
<li><p><strong>What it is</strong>: Returns the entire HTML document as a string, including the <code>&lt;html&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;head&gt;</code>, and <code>&lt;body&gt;</code> tags.</p>
</li>
<li><p><strong>Use case</strong>: To retrieve or replace the complete HTML structure of the document.</p>
</li>
<li><p><strong>Example</strong>: Using the same HTML, <code>document.outerHtml</code> would give you the full <code>&lt;html&gt;&lt;body&gt;&lt;h1&gt;Title&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;Text&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</code>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
